[105.625348, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[105.647905, "o", "An anomaly rule: flag what is far from normal. The simplest kind is a rate rule: normal is a budget.\r\n\r\n  measure   failed sign-ins per account, in its busiest 60 seconds\r\n  normal    at most 5 a minute (config.json, rate.login_fail_per_min)\r\n\r\n  aisha.k      0 failed   normal\r\n"]
[105.648001, "o", "  rohan.v     21 failed   FLAG: more than 5 in 60 s\r\n  tom.r        1 failed   normal\r\n\r\nNo pattern needed: it notices the behaviour, even of an attack nobody has seen before.\r\nIt needs a sense of normal, and a busy honest user can trip it.\r\n"]
[105.651323, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;thesecguy@lab: ~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m23\u0007\u001b[01;32mthesecguy@lab\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m~/ai-security-course-labs/labs/m23\u001b[00m$ "]
